{# Sensor alerts summary - 3.5.

   Every alert the run logged, grouped by severity with the worst first, and
   ordered by time inside each group. A count of each severity heads the
   section. Which alert belongs to which block, and in what order, is
   alert_groups' answer rather than a test made here (5.4).

   2.5 is firm about one thing: nearest_checkpoint_id is spatial proximity and
   not attribution. The column says "Nearest checkpoint" and the section says
   what that means, so no reader takes an alert near a checkpoint for an alert
   caused by one.

   label and description are free text. Autoescaping is on, so a field holding
   <script> or {{ '{{ config }}' }} renders as written (5.5). #}
<section class="section alerts" id="alerts">

  <h2>Sensor alerts</h2>

  {% if alert_groups %}

    <p class="alerts-count">
      {% for severity, total in derived.alerts_by_severity.items() %}
        <span class="alerts-tally">
          <span class="badge badge-small badge-{{ severity | severity_style }}">{{ severity }}</span>
          <span class="alerts-total">{{ total }}</span>
        </span>
      {% endfor %}
    </p>

    <p class="lede">
      Threshold breaches logged during the run, independently of the
      checkpoints. The checkpoint named in each row is the one nearest to where
      the alert was recorded. It is a position, not a cause.
    </p>

    {% for group in alert_groups %}

      <h3>{{ group.severity }} ({{ group.alerts | length }})</h3>

      <table class="data-table alerts-table alerts-{{ group.severity | severity_style }}">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Recorded</th>
            <th>Alert</th>
            <th>Description</th>
            <th>Nearest checkpoint</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for alert in group.alerts %}
            <tr>
              <td>{{ alert.timestamp | moment }}</td>
              <td>
                {{ alert.label | show }}
                <span class="alert-code">{{ alert.code }}</span>
              </td>
              <td>{{ alert.description | show }}</td>
              <td>{{ (alert.nearest_checkpoint_name or alert.nearest_checkpoint_id) | show }}</td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>

    {% endfor %}

  {% else %}
    <p class="absent-note">No sensor alerts were recorded for this run.</p>
  {% endif %}

</section>
